      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T18:11:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Non-blocking comment.\n\nI\u0027m not able to find clear documentation how the \"default\" property for choices and \"depends\" interact or which takes precedence.\n\nI think using the \"default\" property is more common, and I think better illustrates how the choice symbol is used.\n\n```\nchoice SVDM_RSP_CHOICE\n    default SVDM_RSP_DFP_ONLY if !PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_USB4 \u0026\u0026 !PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_TBT_COMPAT_MODE \u0026\u0026 !PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_USB32_DRD\n    default SVDM_RSP_CUSTOM\nendchoice\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 15,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "97125c610fcbcd911c752bd71ac2930bab22b0e9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "adbe0197_ccae990a",
        "filename": "zephyr/Kconfig.svdm_rsp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T23:47:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Linux documentation says that a choice option defaults to the first available option, unless overridden by a default on the choice. I opted to depend on that here because we want to prevent this from being enabled at all if a system uses any of those incompatible options, so the conditions would need to be duplicated above and that seems worse.\n\nIt turns out that (provided the DFP_ONLY choice marks those dependencies) all of these are equivalent:\n\n    # Duplicate conditions for DFP_ONLY\n    default SVDM_RSP_DFP_ONLY if !PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_USB4 \u0026\u0026 !PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_TBT_COMPAT_MODE \u0026\u0026 !PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_USB32_DRD\n    default SVDM_RSP_CUSTOM\n\n    # First default cannot be used since it has unsatisfied dependencies, second is taken\n    default SVDM_RSP_DFP_ONLY\n    default SVDM_RSP_CUSTOM\n\n    # Defaults to first available choice\n    \u003cblank\u003e\n\nSince this could be confusing, I\u0027ve added a comment explaining how it arrives at this default.",
      "parentUuid": "a9cbb7bf_99766c59",
